# Error logging

Use `logger` from `@/logger`. In production `logger.error` reports to Sentry; in dev it echoes to the console. `console.error` never reaches Sentry, so don't pair the two for the same failure.

## Decision table

| Situation | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Caught failure that breaks a feature, corrupts data, or you'd want alerted on | `logger.error` |
| Error already reported at a boundary closer to its source | Don't log again — one report per root cause; callers handle UI/control flow only |
| Expected user-facing outcomes (wrong password, cancelled auth popup, form validation) | UI/toast only; no Sentry |
| Unexpected internal state that validation should have prevented | `logger.error` — signals a real bug, not a user error |
| Caught error swallowed by a fallback (`return []`/`null`) | `logger.error` before returning — an outage shouldn't look like empty results |
| Temporary local debugging while developing | `console.error` (remove or upgrade before merge) |
| CLI / scripts outside `src/` | `console.error` is fine |

## Shape the call

Always wrap the caught error in a new `Error` with a fixed, descriptive message, passing the original via `cause`: this gives a stable Sentry title (one root cause → one issue), preserves the original stack, and sidesteps the `unknown` type of a caught error. Put low-cardinality, filterable labels in `tags` (Sentry indexes them); put IDs/payloads as extra context fields — unique values in `tags` bloat the index instead of aiding search. Common tags: `function` (the function logging the error), `component` (the Vue component, for errors in `.vue` files), and `composable` (the composable, for errors in query/mutation composables).

```ts
// DO — descriptive title + original stack via cause
logger.error(new Error('Failed to fetch administration by ID', { cause: error }), {
  tags: { function: 'fetchAdministrationById' }, // low-cardinality, filterable
  administrationId, // high-cardinality, kept out of tags
});

// DON'T — interpolated message loses the original stack; high-cardinality ID in tags pollutes the index
logger.error(new Error(`Failed: ${error.message}`), { tags: { administrationId } });
```

## No PII in tags or extra

`sendDefaultPii` is disabled app-wide — don't undo that with emails, names, or other identifying free text. Use opaque IDs (uid, administrationId).
